      "result_description": "Tennyson CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "51484",
      "match_notes": "Tennyson put in to bat first started briskly only to lose 1st wicket in the 3rd over. Fine batting by Paul Lewis and Danny Mills gave a great platform for middle order to apply pressure despite B.Patel (28-4) making a brilliant effort to thwart Tennyson advance  specially when JOHN Rogan Blasted out a great 50 in 30 balls giving Tennyson an unassailable 264 runs in their allocated 45 over\u2019s. Rainham weakened by many of their regular 1st team players away on Tour could not cope with the tight bowling by Tennyson despite some resistance by P Margiotta (26) and D Skipper (24) Rainham got skittled out for a meager 120 runs in 35.2 Overs.",
